---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { Content as StandardsBody } from '../copy/standards.md';

/*
 * SOURCE TRACE (Site build 2, Perthos/Research#138)
 *
 * Body: `writing/how-ai-systems-fail/final-standards-how-to-read-an-ai-incident-report.md`
 * in the corpus, generated into `src/copy/standards.md` with its provenance and
 * flag comments stripped. That final applies the 2026-08-22 reconciliation's
 * edit round and the claim rewordings earned by the evaluation-practice-claims
 * run (Perthos/Research#141), which lifted the last blocker on this page.
 *
 * This page is what "this is a call, not a finding" links to, series-wide. Its
 * closing pointer links piece 1; piece 1's first citation of the reading
 * discipline links back here. Both directions are checked at build.
 *
 * Two standing comfort flags are recorded on the corpus file rather than here:
 * the Snyk incentive sentence, and the origin-counting section stating in the
 * operator's own voice that a public count was wrong.
 *
 * Voice: zero em-dashes.
 */
---

<Base
  title="Standards"
  description="How I read an AI incident report, and the rules every piece here is held to."
  ogSlug="standards"
>
  <div class="page-head">
    <h1>How to read an AI incident report</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The rules every piece here is held to, worked through the incidents that
      taught me to ask for them. Published so a reader can hold the writing to
      them.
    </p>
    <hr class="page-head__rule" />
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <StandardsBody />
  </div>
</Base>
